  the bar report again the bar report as  written by William bar references only  investigating conspiracy conspiracy is  only one way in which there could be  coordination or links and its way  narrower than the full scope of what  Robert Muller was looking at and once  again because William bar is summarizing  Moeller's summary and not the evidence  all of the possible evidence for links  and for coordination simply aren't  mentioned by bar bar says conspiracy was  investigated that means agreements of  some kind for illegal purposes you could  have links you could have coordination  and still not have conspiracy bar is  being deceptive by being overly specific  which is a common way that people can  obfuscate underlying evidence and a Seth  Abramson says bar is adopting Trump's  very specific definition of collusion  the narrowest possible definition  referring only to the crime of  conspiracy and says there was an  evidence of that which justified an  indictment this is a sham okay now let  me give you another example of how wacky  we now recognize this four-page report  to be bar starts to mix and confuse  legal language which sounds sort of  innocuous to the average layperson but  it's not okay in the same paragraph of  his report Barr says that Moeller did  not find that the Trump campaign  conspired with or coordinated with  Russia but then when he quotes from  Muller's summary says the investigation  did not establish that members of trumps  campaign conspired establish is a term  with a very specific legal meaning  establish with enough evidence to  justify an indictment or to indicate  that a particular crime has been  committed  did not find witches bars language  suggests  0% evidence if you look at the  underlying case file that molar has  where as did not establish could mean  50% proof could mean 60% proof could  mean 80% proof it could be anything  short of what you would need for an  indictment sort of beyond reasonable  doubt these are legal games